  "creative_intent": {
    "logline": "A runner chasing a race nobody invited him to joins strangers to help a fallen person, discovering a better destination.",
    "hook": "The runner sprints while the city around him appears motionless; he stumbles trying to catch a finish line that no one can see.",
    "theme": "Worth is measured by chosen actions, not other people's pace.",
    "setup_payoff": "The unseen finish line at the beginning is contrasted with the visible community on the way home.",
    "growth_hypothesis": "A silent high-contrast run-to-walk reversal may encourage shares among viewers tired of comparison; unvalidated.",
